Good day Murray,

Thanks for this. With my own (preliminary) data and the log link function, the back-transformed total density (0.001301094) was very similar to the sum of group-specific densities (0.00130501). I didn't try the identity link fix, but would try it if we decide to go this way. I may still go with the CL and derived(), because we will again be fitting many models to many data sets, so it would be nice if we didn't have to fit the same model twice.  However, it's very helpful to have this handy. There may be situations where we want to fit models with spatial covariates of density, so would need to use the FL and model sexes as different groups or sessions.

All the best,
Eric

From u118cea91a1619106 at groups.google.com  Fri Apr 13 02:23:31 2018
